1
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:30,461
This is JoJo's Bizarre Adventure.

2
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:42,740
In the 19th century, as the United States
of America explored its vast continent,

3
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:46,600
the greatest conquest was
that of the western frontier.

4
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:52,860
It beckoned

5
00:00:56,180 --> 00:00:59,840
and a desire called
America sped across the map

6
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:04,880
claiming native lands as its own

7
00:01:05,820 --> 00:01:08,080
till it reached the wide Pacific?

8
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:18,910
Get him!

9
00:01:18,993 --> 00:01:20,417
The bastard's got it coming!

10
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:22,697
He had white men's books
hidden in his tent!

11
00:01:22,780 --> 00:01:23,956
I've seen it myself!

12
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:34,300
How the hell is he so fast?

13
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:37,422
Look, he's running the
same way the white men do!

14
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:40,530
He...

15
00:01:40,613 --> 00:01:41,443
he ran it!

16
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:46,740
It was there, in the west,

17
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:50,080
where the Santa Ana headwinds
blow in from Mexico,

18
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:54,140
that people gathered
in the summer of 1890,

19
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:57,071
every one of them, in search of something.

20
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:17,877
Hey, which one of you left all
that mess in the shitter, huh?

21
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:18,877
It's my tech, you love it!

22
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:19,790
Center trap!

23
00:02:19,873 --> 00:02:20,703
I was here first!

24
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:24,060
Welcome to the first ever Steel Ball Run!

25
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:32,940
This epic trek, which will commence here
in San Diego and end in New York City,

26
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:35,837
will be the first ever
to have its participants

27
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:38,860
cross North America while on horseback!

28
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:44,320
4,000 mind-boggling miles.

29
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:47,180
At the end of the race's nine stages,

30
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:51,380
our victor will receive a
peerless prize of $50 million.

31
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:57,920
Many racers will vie for these riches,
but only one will walk away the winner.

32
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:03,520
A question, Mr. Steele.

33
00:03:04,060 --> 00:03:08,707
Baron Rucatugo from Germany says he
intends to compete from atop an automobile?

34
00:03:08,940 --> 00:03:09,770
Indeed.

35
00:03:09,853 --> 00:03:14,260
and with my blessing for what is
America if not a land of progress.

36
00:03:15,420 --> 00:03:19,655
If he wants to trust a machine, then
that is a good baron's prerogative.

37
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:24,600
The $150 entry fee has been called
a money-making scheme by some.

38
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:26,420
You wound me, sir.

39
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:29,937
We are covering the medical
expenses of any racer

40
00:03:30,020 --> 00:03:32,677
who meets with misfortune
during the endeavor.

41
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:36,240
However, each racer is
responsible for their own safety.

42
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:38,477
We acknowledge their right to bear arms,

43
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:42,177
enshrined as it is within the Second
Amendment of the Constitution.

44
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:45,957
The race will go down as a failure if
no one makes it to the finish line.

45
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:50,275
If that should occur, what do you
think your investors will have to say?

46
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:52,040
Probably just kill me.

47
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:54,380
That was a joke.

48
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:56,110
Okay.

49
00:03:57,060 --> 00:04:00,660
You speak to me of failure,
then I will speak in turn.

50
00:04:01,020 --> 00:04:04,457
There is no failure worse than
turning your back on adventure.

51
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:08,360
To perish in bed untested, having
never faced the impossible?

52
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:09,736
and carried the day.

53
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:13,299
Come what may, this race
is a triumph of the spirit.

54
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:16,397
Our racers don't know
the meaning of failure.

55
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:18,833
No matter how the days ahead may unfold?

56
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:21,497
The steel ball run will be
a race the likes of which!

57
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:23,660
the world has never laid eyes upon.

58
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:30,880
What am I gonna do, Lucy?

59
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:33,100
I'm so scared right now.

60
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,057
What if the whole thing falls apart?

61
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:37,560
It's all my fault!

62
00:04:38,780 --> 00:04:40,160
Steven, you'll be okay.

63
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:44,249
After all, you've been a promoter
for 40 years, haven't you?

64
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:46,120
Have faith, sweetheart.

65
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:48,160
I know it'll all work out.

66
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,820
Okay, I'll try to be brave.

67
00:04:53,620 --> 00:04:54,450
Atta boy.

68
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:10,964
Okay, I'm guessing you're here to
sign up for the race, ain't ya?

69
00:05:11,380 --> 00:05:13,086
Gonna need your John Hancock.

70
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:17,558
We'll take your fingerprints and
horse's nose prints on the first day.

71
00:05:17,660 --> 00:05:21,601
Just know you can't swap out the
jockey or the horse down the road.

72
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:24,094
Taddlecloth and your entry certificate.

73
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:25,990
Hmm?

74
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:33,030
Gyrocephaly.

75
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:35,450
Oh, oh.

76
00:05:35,533 --> 00:05:36,363
Neil?

77
00:05:36,446 --> 00:05:37,276
Oh.

78
00:05:37,359 --> 00:05:38,189
Oh.

79
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:41,300
Those are some unusual
baubles you got there.

80
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:44,628
They do something or
are they just for show?

81
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:46,710
Ah!

82
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:50,110
Oh!

83
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:55,200
My legs.

84
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:56,717
What did you...

85
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:57,720
Damn it!

86
00:05:57,880 --> 00:05:59,197
What did you do to me, huh?

87
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:01,497
I was just curious about
those balls or whatever.

88
00:06:01,580 --> 00:06:05,797
I didn't mean no harm
that right hey clerk how

89
00:06:05,880 --> 00:06:08,857
much of my entry fee is
on the counter huh if

90
00:06:08,940 --> 00:06:11,237
the money's all there
why then I guess I've got

91
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:13,237
no quarrel with you oh

92
00:06:13,320 --> 00:06:18,317
you came up short $20 but

93
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:21,137
I did pay the full amount
didn't I still hadn't

94
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:23,637
given you your receipt
nothing's official till

95
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:27,177
I do I wonder where that
cash might have run off

96
00:06:27,260 --> 00:06:30,017
to you're going to give
back what you pilfered?

97
00:06:30,100 --> 00:06:33,597
Because if you don't, they won't
let me compete in the race.

98
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:35,562
And that would mean I don't win.

99
00:06:35,860 --> 00:06:36,690
Understand?

100
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:39,860
Oh, he's a thief!

101
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:41,800
Security, come quick!

102
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:43,806
Just give me my damn receipt.

103
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:53,000
What happened?

104
00:06:53,260 --> 00:06:54,436
Caught him thieving.

105
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:57,320
Hey, Valkyrie.

106
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:58,718
Sorry for the wait.

107
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:02,517
Time to find a tent and make
myself at home for a while.

108
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:03,718
Look at me, dammit!

109
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:05,197
I ain't done with you yet!

110
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:06,340
No way, no how!

111
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:10,017
Whatever shit you pulled in there,
I'd like to see you try that again!

112
00:07:10,100 --> 00:07:11,276
Quit your wriggling!

113
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:12,990
See that?

114
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:14,100
Now you die!

115
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:17,377
Man, fool's got a hold of my gun!

116
00:07:17,460 --> 00:07:18,342
Little bastard!

117
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:23,280
Food for thought, Goldteeth!

118
00:07:23,380 --> 00:07:26,380
If I wanted you dead, you'd
be warm food right now!

119
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:30,637
Well, you act all high and mighty, but
you never saw me grabbing those coins!

120
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:33,797
I got the law sicked on me
for nothing more than a guess!

121
00:07:33,880 --> 00:07:35,640
And that I cannot abide!

122
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:37,240
Good news, pal!

123
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:38,597
I'm joining the race!

124
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:40,798
That way you'll never see me coming!

125
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:45,480
Only thing you're joining is a
chain gang. Enough. Let him go.

126
00:07:46,020 --> 00:07:46,850
Huh?

127
00:07:47,460 --> 00:07:49,020
I'm not pressing charges.

128
00:07:49,300 --> 00:07:50,359
Don't lock him up.

129
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:51,951
There's no need for that.

130
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:54,140
Let him go.

131
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:55,840
And give him a gun.

132
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:16,240
Pick it up take it take it
and see what happens next.

133
00:08:21,220 --> 00:08:23,797
We're out of our league
here where's the sheriff?

134
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:26,420
I think we're about to see some bloodshed.

135
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:29,540
What's all the fuss about? Hey!

136
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:31,388
Get out of the way already!

137
00:08:31,740 --> 00:08:33,220
I can't see a damn thing!

138
00:08:43,420 --> 00:08:44,320
Come on!

139
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:47,037
You didn't think I
meant all that, did you?

140
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:48,820
I was kidding! No harm done!

141
00:08:50,060 --> 00:08:53,260
I, uh, I don't much like the
way you're looking at me.

142
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:55,610
See?

143
00:08:55,693 --> 00:08:57,718
I wasn't gonna hurt you none honest.

144
00:08:58,220 --> 00:09:00,280
Yeah, best of luck in the race.

145
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:01,760
Nobody move.

146
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:03,628
Just one of you boys up to.

147
00:09:17,340 --> 00:09:19,164
You're lucky I didn't do worse.

148
00:09:19,700 --> 00:09:22,217
I would find a doctor for
that arm if I were you.

149
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:24,418
And drop the gun while you're at it.

150
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:25,873
Somebody could get hurt

151
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:41,180
Sheriff what do we do now?

152
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:44,280
Just another duel nothing
to lose sleep over a

153
00:09:45,260 --> 00:09:48,280
Duel both men agreed to so it goes.

154
00:09:49,780 --> 00:09:51,160
Duel my ass.

155
00:09:51,820 --> 00:09:53,702
I'm not even sure what happened.

156
00:09:55,140 --> 00:09:56,457
That ball he threw.

157
00:09:56,540 --> 00:09:58,160
It was spinning fast.

158
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:01,557
So fast that it dug right into his arm.

159
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:04,040
And even that didn't slow it down.

160
00:10:05,820 --> 00:10:07,017
Hey, wait up.

161
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:08,806
What's that steel ball about?

162
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:10,437
I need to see it again.

163
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:11,897
Hand it over. No, don't.

164
00:10:11,980 --> 00:10:13,686
It's still spinning, damn it!

165
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:27,300
What was that?

166
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:29,020
My legs.

167
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:30,637
Just then I was...

168
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:32,040
I was standing.

169
00:10:36,540 --> 00:10:38,020
No! Wait!

170
00:10:39,620 --> 00:10:40,760
Let me through!

171
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:42,700
Get out of my way!

172
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,791
Move it, you old bastard!

173
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:45,857
What'd you come from?

174
00:10:45,940 --> 00:10:46,770
Shut up!

175
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:48,330
Please!

176
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,217
What did you do to me?

177
00:10:51,300 --> 00:10:53,077
I need to know what that was just now!

178
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:54,757
You're gonna tell me everything!

179
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:57,140
Top cause of death. Wanna take a guess?

180
00:10:58,920 --> 00:11:01,517
Mosquito-borne diseases
are killer number one.

181
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:04,777
But getting kicked by a horse
is definitely the runner-up.

182
00:11:04,860 --> 00:11:08,448
You trying to get him to switch
places on the podium or what?

183
00:11:08,580 --> 00:11:10,740
Don't get your hopes up. I mean it.

184
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:15,037
You standing up from that chair
was nothing more than coincidence.

185
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:17,140
A muscle spasm, that's all.

186
00:11:17,240 --> 00:11:18,100
A spasm?

187
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,960
It was the steel ball. I know it!

188
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:23,577
Please let me touch it again!

189
00:11:23,660 --> 00:11:24,540
I can pay you!

190
00:11:24,660 --> 00:11:26,954
I'm done with this little conversation.

191
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:35,240
Hey, you mouthy brat.

192
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:37,837
Did you think I was
going to let that slide?

193
00:11:37,920 --> 00:11:40,200
Well, all right then.

194
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:46,584
If you won't hand over the ball
to me, I'll take it my dance now!

195
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:56,840
My fingers!

196
00:11:57,560 --> 00:12:00,297
I guess there's no harm in
giving you a bit of credit.

197
00:12:00,380 --> 00:12:03,517
You're sporting some pretty
well-conditioned muscles up above,

198
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:05,071
quite a feat considering.

199
00:12:05,260 --> 00:12:07,084
But it doesn't change anything.

200
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:10,917
The spin of the steel balls won't
magically let you walk again.

201
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,037
They can't just give you your legs back.

202
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:15,817
I'm supposed to believe that
after what I've seen them do?

203
00:12:15,900 --> 00:12:19,457
No matter what it takes, I'm going to
figure out the mystery of the spin!

204
00:12:19,540 --> 00:12:23,480
When you can't even ride a horse,
I'll be gone in two days' time.

205
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:26,917
Got a cross-country
race that needs winning.

206
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Hey, come on! Damn it all!

207
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:37,540
Who's in the way now, huh?

208
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:41,857
Maybe you'll watch your mouth
next time, you little shit.

209
00:12:41,940 --> 00:12:43,840
Scram already. Roll on home.

210
00:13:02,420 --> 00:13:05,560
I wonder why I came to
this beach in San Diego.

211
00:13:07,300 --> 00:13:10,535
Was it just to witness the
start of the steel ball run?

212
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:12,640
Or was it?

213
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:18,840
My name is Johnny Joestar.

214
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:22,820
My father was a rancher and
a well-known horse trainer.

215
00:13:24,060 --> 00:13:26,920
So all of my life, horses
have been by my side.

216
00:13:29,220 --> 00:13:32,102
Watching their muscles
work from atop the saddle,

217
00:13:32,220 --> 00:13:34,437
hearing their hooves strike the ground?

218
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:35,640
it was beautiful.

219
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:40,337
Whenever they ran, it felt like I could
understand their thoughts and emotions.

220
00:13:40,420 --> 00:13:42,067
Like we shared a connection.

221
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:46,315
Beautiful things demand our attention.

222
00:13:46,900 --> 00:13:51,840
And if it's something dynamic and alive,
too, there's nothing more captivating.

223
00:13:52,860 --> 00:13:54,980
Young master Johnny has talent.

224
00:13:55,340 --> 00:13:58,420
So said the old stable
hand, and I believed him.

225
00:13:58,760 --> 00:14:00,700
But my father remained aloof.

226
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:05,060
For my older brother Nicholas
was already a rising star.

227
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:09,200
Until an accident
claimed his life one day.

228
00:14:11,060 --> 00:14:12,620
and everything changed.

229
00:14:14,820 --> 00:14:19,640
After his death, I began racing horses
in earnest and won time and time again.

230
00:14:20,660 --> 00:14:22,660
They started calling me a prodigy.

231
00:14:23,660 --> 00:14:27,013
With each new victory, more
people would gravitate to me,

232
00:14:27,140 --> 00:14:30,669
paying homage with their flattery,
their gifts, their money.

233
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:34,152
To win a race on horseback was a triumph.

234
00:14:34,460 --> 00:14:38,740
Mastering oneself and the beast
below, it felt like manifest destiny.

235
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:42,757
But destiny had something else in mind.

236
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:44,577
Just you wait.

237
00:14:44,660 --> 00:14:47,857
Once you see how dazzling she is,
you won't make fun of me anymore.

238
00:14:47,940 --> 00:14:49,657
Is Dorothy Parker that great?

239
00:14:49,740 --> 00:14:50,937
I'm telling you, Johnny.

240
00:14:51,020 --> 00:14:54,577
The day will come when the world
treats actresses like works of art.

241
00:14:54,660 --> 00:14:57,537
I guess that would explain the
crowd I've been waiting in line.

242
00:14:57,620 --> 00:14:58,450
You know?

243
00:14:58,533 --> 00:15:03,057
Yeah, so I've been in
line since yesterday.

244
00:15:03,140 --> 00:15:04,217
Oh yeah.

245
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:05,535
And look what it got.

246
00:15:05,980 --> 00:15:07,737
The end of the line is back there!

247
00:15:07,820 --> 00:15:08,877
I've been here all night!

248
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:09,817
You can't just cut in!

249
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:11,277
You need to shut up already!

250
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:13,697
No one gives a shit that
you pulled an all-nighter!

251
00:15:13,780 --> 00:15:15,537
Hey, someone had better
tell me what's going on.

252
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:19,817
I was standing in line fair and square when
this guy walked up and tried to cut in.

253
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:20,730
What?

254
00:15:20,813 --> 00:15:22,840
By the way, this is Johnny Joestar.

255
00:15:27,100 --> 00:15:29,218
I knew you were the coolest, Johnny!

256
00:15:29,980 --> 00:15:31,957
Seriously, is this
thing worth the trouble?

257
00:15:32,040 --> 00:15:33,160
Aw, come on!

258
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:36,460
You again?

259
